<details class='srcweek' open><summary>Quantum <span class='count'>3</span></summary><ul class='events plain newslist'><li class="evrow newsrow" data-detail="{&quot;fields&quot;: [[&quot;Headline&quot;, &quot;Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle&quot;], [&quot;Source&quot;, &quot;arXiv quant-ph · Thu, 06 Aug 2026 00:00&quot;], [&quot;Summary&quot;, &quot;arXiv:2608.04055v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: The minimum change principle provides an information-theoretic characterization of the Bayes reversal channel in classical probability theory and has recently been proposed as a framework for extending Bayes&#x27; rule to quantum information theory. Using quantum relative entropy, we investigate a minimum change principle for the setting of quantum statis&quot;]], &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04055&quot;}" data-key="news|Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle"><button class="flagbtn" data-flag="news|Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle" data-flabel="Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle" data-fkind="news" data-fpayload="{&quot;title&quot;: &quot;Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;: &quot;arXiv:2608.04055v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: The minimum change principle provides an information-theoretic characterization of the Bayes reversal channel in classical probability theory and has recently been proposed as a framework for extending Bayes&#x27; rule to quantum information theory. Using quantum relative entropy, we investigate a minimum change principle for the setting of quantum statis&quot;, &quot;link&quot;: &quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04055&quot;, &quot;source&quot;: &quot;arXiv quant-ph&quot;, &quot;date&quot;: &quot;Thu, 06 Aug 2026 00:00&quot;}" title="flag for Wed">&#9873;</button><div class="nbody"><div class="nhead">Unifying quantum measurement constructions via a relative-entropy minimum change principle</div><div class="ntake">arXiv:2608.04055v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: The minimum change principle provides an information-theoretic characterization of the Bayes</div></div></li><li class="evrow newsrow" data-detail="{&quot;fields&quot;: [[&quot;Headline&quot;, &quot;Graph-Aware Exact Branch-and-Bound with Device Profiles for Static Qubit Allocation&quot;], [&quot;Source&quot;, &quot;arXiv quant-ph · Thu, 06 Aug 2026 00:00&quot;], [&quot;Summary&quot;, &quot;arXiv:2608.04058v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Static qubit allocation maps a circuit&#x27;s logical qubits to a sparse physical device while minimising an interaction-weighted physical-distance cost function, yielding a rectangular quadratic assignment problem. Existing work combines strong lower bounds with distributed branch-and-bound. We integrate graph-aware exact reductions with an engineering b&quot;]], &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04058&quot;}" data-key="news|Graph-Aware Exact Branch-and-Bound with Device Profiles for Static Qubit Allocation"><button class="flagbtn" data-flag="news|Graph-Aware Exact Branch-and-Bound with Device Profiles for Static Qubit Allocation" data-flabel="Graph-Aware Exact Branch-and-Bound with Device Profiles for Static Qubit Allocation" data-fkind="news" data-fpayload="{&quot;title&quot;: &quot;Graph-Aware Exact Branch-and-Bound with Device Profiles for Static Qubit Allocation&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;: &quot;arXiv:2608.04058v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Static qubit allocation maps a circuit&#x27;s logical qubits to a sparse physical device while minimising an interaction-weighted physical-distance cost function, yielding a rectangular quadratic assignment problem. Existing work combines strong lower bounds with distributed branch-and-bound. We integrate graph-aware exact reductions with an